# K03 NS-ROLES-2 (Codex K03-NS-ROLES-2-20261007-20; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md#resolved-head-consumption,
# #declaration-visibility): a named Structure's body takes the common roles of the root and a method.
# `Count()`, `Count: ()` and bare `Count` in Host's body are Count's one nullary call each, run when Host runs:
# three calls of Count, whose statement adds one to Tally's k.  Exit 7; 81 if a call ran at Host's construction, 82
# if a spelling did not call.
Tally:
    int: k 0
end: Tally
Count:
    Tally\k: Tally\k + 1
end: Count
Host:
    Count()
    Count: ()
    Count
end: Host
fn: m () int
    if: Tally\k != 0
        return: 81
    Host()
    if: Tally\k != 3
        return: 82
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
